{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROUND 1: BLOCK, four findings. ALL ACCEPTED, and two of them are my errors rather than gaps in the plan's ambition.\n\nFINDINGS 1, 3 and 4 ARE ONE THEME: src/rebar/_deprecations.py was missing from the SCOPE section. I had put it in file_impact and then failed to name it in Scope — an internal inconsistency in my own ticket. And the omission mattered, because the codebase ENFORCES the mechanism rather than merely offering it:\n  * registration goes through _scheduled(...) into REGISTRY (_deprecations.py:62, :100);\n  * emission goes through warn_deprecated (:299);\n  * tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py:125::test_no_raw_deprecation_emissions SOURCE-SCANS all of src/rebar/ and fails any deprecation signal that does not route through warn_deprecated.\nSo the plan as written — 'emit a deprecation warning in config.py' — would have failed an existing test, AND been invisible to scripts/gen_env_registry.py, which imports rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY and unions it into the generated env docs. Scope now states all of that with citations.\n\nFINDING 2 IS THE ONE WORTH DWELLING ON: my 'MEASURED five files' enumeration was INCOMPLETE, and I had labelled it MEASURED. The review pointed at README.md:239. Re-measured across the WHOLE repo: there are SIX prose files, not five —\n  README.md, docs/llm-framework.md, docs/config.md, docs/plan-review-gate.md,\n  docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md, docs/env-vars.md (generated).\nThe one I missed is the PROJECT FRONT PAGE, and it is the most consequential of the six: README.md:239 presents REBAR_LLM_MODEL as THE documented multi-provider interface ('plus Gemini and OpenAI-compatible local servers like LMStudio/Ollama via REBAR_LLM_MODEL/...'). A deprecation ticket that missed it would have left the front door advertising the deprecated lever.\n\nWHY I MISSED IT, because the mechanism is reusable and so is the mistake: I ran the grep scoped to `docs/ infra/` and wrote MEASURED against the result. The measurement was real; its SCOPE was wrong. Labelling something MEASURED does not make it COMPLETE — the scope of the measurement is part of the claim, and a repo-root file falls outside every subdirectory grep. This is the third time this session that a confidently-stated fact was wrong in a way only re-running it exposed (the others: plan_review_recovery.py:8's docstring, which is accurate, and a d23e 'circular dependency' that evaporated).\n\nBoth fixes applied; re-review running."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785583396924456001,"uuid":"960a873b-ecab-4c34-ab52-f6cbfbc205fe"}